                           && request.resource.data.totalMoves > 0\
                           && request.resource.data.totalMoves < 100000;\
             allow update, delete: if false;\
           \}\
         \}\
       \}\
\
     This lets anyone read the leaderboard and add a new score, but nobody\
     can edit or delete existing scores, and scores must look like real\
     scores (right shape, sane range) rather than arbitrary data.\
\
  4. Go to Project settings (gear icon) -> General -> "Your apps" -> Web app\
     (</> icon) -> register the app -> copy the firebaseConfig object it\
     gives you -> paste it below, replacing the placeholder values.\
  5. Commit and push \'97 GitHub Pages will pick it up automatically.\
  ===========================================================================\
